Package: gh0st
Version: @GH0ST_VERSION@
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: Gh0st OS <15324879+therezor@users.noreply.github.com>
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Depends: gh0st-panel-modules, xdg-user-dirs, network-manager, wireplumber, pulseaudio-utils,
 bluez, rfkill, pkexec, polkitd, libpam-modules-bin, raspi-utils-core, passwd, apt,
 iw, dnsmasq-base, nftables, curl, sqv, libarchive-tools, openssh-client, bubblewrap,
 sudo, libpam-runtime, libpam-modules, gh0st-base (>= @BASE_VERSION@)
Provides: applaunch (= 0.6.111)
Conflicts: applaunch
Replaces: applaunch
Description: the Gh0st OS shell and Settings
 The home screen, switcher and OS bars (gh0st shell), Files (gh0st-files),
 Text (gh0st-text), gh0st open and xdg-open, Settings
 (gh0st-settings), Updates (gh0st-update and the update engine), the
 Store (gh0st-store and its engine), the keyring and session services
 (gh0st keyring, gh0st session) with the Keyring app (gh0st-keyring), and
 the root helper. Static binaries;
 the Depends are the commands they run: nmcli, wpctl, pactl, pacat, rfkill,
 pkexec, vcgencmd, unix_chkpwd, passwd, iw, and systemd's systemctl,
 timedatectl and hostnamectl. Settings and Keyboard talk to bluetoothd
 (bluez) on the system bus. dnsmasq-base and nftables are what
 NetworkManager's shared mode runs for the hotspot: DHCP and DNS, and NAT.
 The Store's engine fetches with curl and checks the app list with sqv.
 Files opens archives with bsdtar (libarchive-tools) and reaches servers
 with ssh (openssh-client). Apps run sandboxed in bwrap (bubblewrap), under
 gh0st-base's bus policy and audio rules. An app that asks for root goes
 through sudo; the PAM profile lets one the user allowed past the password
 (pam-auth-update, from libpam-runtime; pam_exec, from libpam-modules).
 .
 The shell is the launcher stock apps name as applaunch: it keeps the
 stock launcher's app contract, so it provides that name in its place.
